      "id": 1,
      "text": "In the early 1900s, People’s Natural Gas Company built a cooling system on Dunkard Creek to keep its Brave compressor station running.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brave%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The system used pipes buried at the creek’s bottom and two dams to maintain a steady water flow for cooling the gas.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brave%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "After the compressor station shut down in 1959, the cooling apparatus remained, later causing environmental problems in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brave%2C_Pennsylvania"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Brave sits in Pennsylvania’s southwestern corner, just a stone’s throw from the West Virginia border.",
